    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="instruction-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">MOV (array to vector, four registers)</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Move four ZA single-vector groups to Z four-vector operand</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction operates on four ZA single-vector groups.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">The single-vector group within each quarter
of the ZA array is selected by the sum of the vector select register and offset, modulo
quarter the number of ZA array vectors.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">The vector group symbol VGx4
indicates that the instruction operates on four ZA single-vector groups.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">The preferred disassembly syntax uses a 64-bit element size, but an assembler should accept
any element size if it is used consistently for all operands. The vector group symbol is
preferred for disassembly, but optional in assembler source code.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction is unpredicated.</p>
    <p>
        This is an alias of
        <a href="mova_mz_za4.html">MOVA (array to vector, four registers)</a>.
        This means:
      </p><ul><li>
          The encodings in this description are named to match the encodings of
          <a href="mova_mz_za4.html">MOVA (array to vector, four registers)</a>.
        </li><li>The description of <a href="mova_mz_za4.html">MOVA (array to vector, four registers)</a> gives the operational pseudocode, any <span class="arm-defined-word">constrained unpredictable</span> behavior, and any operational information for this instruction.</li></ul>
    <h3 class="classheading"><a id="iclass_sme2"></a>SME2 class
        <span style="font-size:smaller;"><br></br>(FEAT_SME2)
          </span></h3><p class="desc"></p><div class="regdiagram-32"><table class="regdiagram"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr">1</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="lr">0</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">0</td><td>0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="lr">1</td><td class="lr">1</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td colspan="2" class="lr">Rv</td><td class="l">0</td><td>1</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td colspan="3" class="lr">off3</td><td colspan="3" class="lr">Zd</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">0</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="encoding"><div class="encoding__label"><h4 class="encoding">Encoding</h4><a id="mov_mz_za4_1_mova_mz_za4_1"></a></div><p class="asm-code">MOV  { <a href="#Zd1__2" title='Is the name of the first scalable vector register of the destination multi-vector group, encoded as "Zd" times 4.'>&lt;Zd1&gt;</a>.D-<a href="#Zd4" title='Is the name of the fourth scalable vector register of the destination multi-vector group, encoded as "Zd" times 4 plus 3.'>&lt;Zd4&gt;</a>.D }, ZA.D[<a href="#Wv" title='Is the 32-bit name of the vector select register W8-W11, encoded as "Rv" plus 8.'>&lt;Wv&gt;</a>, <a href="#offs" title='Is the vector select offset, in the range 0 to 7, encoded in the "off3" field.'>&lt;offs&gt;</a>{, VGx4}]</p><p class="equivto">
      is equivalent to
    </p>
          <p class="asm-code"><a href="mova_mz_za4.html#mova_mz_za4_1">MOVA</a>  { <a href="mova_mz_za4.html#Zd1__2">&lt;Zd1&gt;</a>.D-<a href="mova_mz_za4.html#Zd4">&lt;Zd4&gt;</a>.D }, ZA.D[<a href="mova_mz_za4.html#Wv">&lt;Wv&gt;</a>, <a href="mova_mz_za4.html#offs">&lt;offs&gt;</a>{, VGx4}]</p>
          <p class="equivto">
          and is always the preferred disassembly.
        </p>
        </div>
  <div class="encoding-notes"></div><h2 class="explanations">Assembler Symbols</h2><div class="explanations"><table><col class="asyn-l"></col><col class="asyn-r"></col><tr><td>&lt;Zd1&gt;</td><td><a id="Zd1__2"></a>
        
          <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">Is the name of the first scalable vector register of the destination multi-vector group, encoded as "Zd" times 4.</p>
        
      </td></tr></table><table><col class="asyn-l"></col><col class="asyn-r"></col><tr><td>&lt;Zd4&gt;</td><td><a id="Zd4"></a>
        
          <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">Is the name of the fourth scalable vector register of the destination multi-vector group, encoded as "Zd" times 4 plus 3.</p>
        
      </td></tr></table><table><col class="asyn-l"></col><col class="asyn-r"></col><tr><td>&lt;Wv&gt;</td><td><a id="Wv"></a>
        
          <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">Is the 32-bit name of the vector select register W8-W11, encoded as "Rv" plus 8.</p>
        
      </td></tr></table><table><col class="asyn-l"></col><col class="asyn-r"></col><tr><td>&lt;offs&gt;</td><td><a id="offs"></a>
        
          <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">Is the vector select offset, in the range 0 to 7, encoded in the "off3" field.</p>
        
      </td></tr></table></div><div class="syntax-notes"></div><div class="alias_ps_section"><h3 class="pseudocode">Operation</h3><p>The description of <a href="mova_mz_za4.html">MOVA (array to vector, four registers)</a> gives the operational pseudocode for this instruction.</p></div><div class="alias_ps_section"><h3 class="pseudocode">Operational Information</h3><p>The description of <a href="mova_mz_za4.html">MOVA (array to vector, four registers)</a> gives the operational information for this instruction.</p></div><hr class="bottom_line"></hr><p class="copyconf">Version 2026.09 — Copyright © 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates.</p><small>This site is provided as a community resource and is NOT affiliated with nor endorsed by Arm Limited.</small><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --><script defer src='https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js' data-cf-beacon='{"token": "de55e78a4e194365a81a0724c5c0ee91"}'></script><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --></body></html>
